@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import {
  delegation, brief text,
}
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import {
    task, task id, brief, child run, result, transcript, launch spec, attach command,
  session export, child driver, child session, starter tools,
}
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import {
    project root, unknown agent error, load error, general agent, fallback agent,
  agent definition,
        agent file, starter entries, timeout, thinking level, model, default tier,
  agents map, tool list,
}
@design/kernel.sigil from Kernel import {
  driver registry, parent adapter, supported host, entry point, host,
}
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import {
    task record, task status, parent session id, start-up sweep,
}

component Cli {
  goal {
    Give a person at a terminal the same delegation as the MCP server, plus a way
    to open and export what a child did after the parent session is gone.
  }

  logic {
    Every command starts through the delegation service, so that the
    start-up sweep runs first. On subzero run, make a delegation from the agent
    name given with the agent option, which may be left out, and the brief text in
    the arguments, with no parent session id, wait
    for
    it
    and print the result. When no agent name is given or the agent name is general,
    and no general agent is configured, or when the agent name is a name other than
    general that the agents map does not hold and no fallback agent is configured,
    print the unknown agent error to stderr and exit non-zero with no task made.
    When a fallback agent is configured, a name other than general that the agents
    map does not hold runs the fallback agent and the printed result says that the
    named
    agent is not configured. When the
    agent file fails to load, print the load error to stderr and exit non-zero
    the same way. On subzero init, take a model from the arguments and, from named
    options, a host, a timeout that defaults to 1200 seconds and a thinking level
    that defaults to medium, where the host option may be left out when exactly one
    supported host is registered, and ask the driver registry for the
    starter tools of the child driver of that host. Then ask AgentConfig to add the
    starter entries to the agent file under the project root that the delegation
    service resolved: the default tier with that host, that model and that
    thinking level, a general agent with the tool list for a general agent and a
    fallback agent with the tool list that only reads, both with that timeout, and
    print which entries it added and
    which it found already there. Refuse with a message that says no host is
    registered when the driver registry lists none, refuse with a message that
    names every supported host when the host is missing and several are registered,
    or is not a supported
    host, refuse with a message that names the host when its child driver offers no
    starter tools, and print the load error and exit non-zero when the agent file
    exists and does not load for a reason other than a missing default tier, and
    print the error that names both hosts and exit
    non-zero when the agent file already holds a default tier on another host than
    the given host. On subzero tasks, read the task record of each task
    and print
    the
    id,
    agent, task status and creation time of every task. On subzero attach, read
    the launch spec of the task, refuse when the task has no recorded
    launch spec or its child run is live, and otherwise ask the driver registry for
    the attach command of the child driver of the host of the agent definition of
    the task, start it, and refuse with a message that names the host when that
    child driver offers none. On subzero show, export the child session of the task
    through the session export of the child driver of the host of the task,
    refusing with a message that names the host when that child driver offers none,
    and say that an abandoned task has no result. Each
    command ends by printing its output and exiting.
  }

  constraints {
    The Cli passes its working directory to the delegation service as its fallback
    project root, and receives from the delegation service the project root that it
    resolved, which comes from AgentConfig in the order its constraints give, for
    its own use by init.

    A delegation from the Cli must carry no parent session id, because a command
    line has no conversation.

    The attach command must be refused while the task status of the task is
    running, because the start-up sweep has already marked the task of a dead
    owner abandoned. It must also be refused with a message that no launch spec
    was recorded when the task record has none.

    Cli depends on DelegationService for the delegation, the status line and
    the result text that it prints, on TaskStore for the
    task record, on TaskCore for the launch spec, the attach command and the
    session export, on AgentConfig for the agent file, the starter entries and the
    errors it shows, and on the driver registry of Kernel for the child driver of a
    host. Cli must not depend on any particular child driver or parent adapter, and
    it names no host. The entry point of the command line process is outside Cli:
    it imports the child drivers that process needs and registers them with Kernel,
    and Cli imports none of them.
  }

  cases {
    Attach on a task whose task status is running is refused. On a settled task it
    asks the driver registry for the attach command of the child driver of its host
    and builds it from the launch spec, and on a task with no recorded launch spec
    it is refused. When the child driver of its host offers no attach command, it
    is refused with a message that names the host.

    Subzero run against a scripted pi writes the task record with task.json,
    events.jsonl and turns/1.json, appends an index line and prints the result.

    Subzero run with an unknown agent name and no fallback agent prints the
    unknown agent error and exits non-zero without making a task. Subzero run with
    no agent name runs the general agent. Subzero init with the host pi, in an
    agent file whose default tier is on the host claude, prints the error that
    names both hosts, exits non-zero and writes nothing.

    Subzero init in a project with no agent file creates the agent file with a
    default tier on the one registered host, the given model and the thinking level
    medium, and a general agent and a read-only fallback agent, each with a timeout
    of 1200 seconds. Run again, it adds nothing, changes no line and says that all
    three entries are already there. With a general agent already in the file, it
    adds only the fallback
    agent and leaves the general agent as it was.
  }

  interface {
    Offer five commands: subzero init with a model and the named options host,
    timeout and thinking, subzero run with a brief and the named option agent,
    which may be left out,
    subzero tasks, subzero attach with a task id,
    and subzero show with a task id.

    Make the child session of a task, its transcript and its task record reachable
    by task id after the parent session has ended.
  }
}
